      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Explanation of Process**\n",
        "\n",
        "In this table, we are trying to show each directors count of movies directed along with the mean, median, and std of age differences. I also made sure to only include directors that have directed 3 or more movies so that we can both get a mean and median that is not just from 1 or 2 movies. I also believe that if a director has directed 3 movies or more, it means that they have been successful. This is different from what we did before as in our proposal we did not dropna nor did we exclude any directors if they have directed enough movies. This matters for analysis because it gives us a more accurate representation on how each director chooses to pair his love interest. I also decided to order the directors age difference from largest to smallest. The range was betweeen 2.40 and 30."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "b1gv87VtP0Je"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Categorical** **to** **Numerical**\n",
        "\n",
        "In order to run a clustering, I needed to transform character gender to an integer. The first 4 lines of the code, standarizes these columns and creates a new pairing column. Then the next line of code, checks to see if the pairing column equals a specific column, then converts the result into 1 or 0, which creates a new numeric indicator column.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Zp5kwPa-SoU3"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "age[\"pairing\"] = (\n",
        "    age[\"character_1_gender\"].astype(str).str.strip().str.lower()\n",
        "    + \"–\" +\n",
        "    age[\"character_2_gender\"].astype(str).str.strip().str.lower()\n",
        ")\n",
        "age['OM']=(age['pairing']=='man–woman').astype(int)\n",
        "age['OF']=(age['pairing']=='man-woman').astype(int)\n",
        "age['Male_Male']=(age['pairing']=='man-man').astype(int)\n",
        "age['Female_Female']=(age['pairing']=='woman-woman').astype(int)\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "-eD9wcab9Try"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Director Level Features to KMeans**\n",
        "Here I decided to group all rows by director and display summary stats. Then I made sure to drop all directors with missing values. Once I dropped the missing values I created the feature matrix and standardized the features. Then I fit the K-means and assign clusters"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "_6HlL455U-SM"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "dir_features=(age.groupby('director').agg(Avg_Gap=('age_difference','mean'),Std_Gap=('age_difference','std'),OM=('OM','mean'),OF=('OF','mean'),Male_Male=('Male_Male','mean'), Female_Female=('Female_Female','mean')).reset_index())\n",
        "dir_features = dir_features.dropna()\n",
        "X=dir_features.drop(columns=['director'])\n",
        "scaler=StandardScaler()\n",
        "X_scaled=scaler.fit_transform(X)\n",
        "kmeans=KMeans(n_clusters=3,random_state=42)\n",
        "dir_features['cluster']=kmeans.fit_predict(X_scaled)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6rlgx9S9V23N"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
